      "message": "In `util/focaltech/ft_log.h`, when `FT_LOG_DIS` is defined, the macros expand to nothing:\n\n```c\n#define FT_LOGE(fmt, ...)\n\n```\n\nEmpty macros are notorious for causing subtle logic bugs if used within single-statement `if/else` blocks lacking braces. If `FT_LOGE` expands to nothing, the *next* line of code accidentally becomes the body of the `if` statement.\n\n* **Remediation:** Define disabled macros as `do {} while (0)` or `(void)0` to ensure syntactic safety.\n\n```c\n#define FT_LOGE(fmt, ...) do {} while (0)\n\n```",
