      "writtenOn": "2026-06-15T23:13:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gemini instructions (double check for correctness):\n\n----\n\nHere are all the necessary changes to implement the `size_t` interface purity refactoring. By making these changes, the custom transport layer strictly deals in standard C++ sizes, and the dirty `libusb` `int` cast is isolated to the single file that actually calls the C library.\n\n### 1. `util/focaltech/usb_transport.h`\n\nUpdate the abstract interface to return `size_t`.\n\n```cpp\n// Change return types from int to size_t\nvirtual std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Send(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data,\n                                          std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) \u003d 0;\nvirtual std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Recv(std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data,\n                                          std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) \u003d 0;\n\n```\n\n### 2. `util/focaltech/usb_device.h`\n\nUpdate the wrapper class methods.\n\n```cpp\n// Change return types from int to size_t\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Send(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data,\n                                  std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) const {\n  return transport_-\u003eSend(data, timeout);\n}\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Recv(std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data,\n                                  std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) const {\n  return transport_-\u003eRecv(data, timeout);\n}\n\n```\n\n### 3. `util/focaltech/libusb_transport.h`\n\nUpdate the concrete implementation signatures.\n\n```cpp\n// Change return types from int to size_t\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Send(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data,\n                                  std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) override;\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Recv(std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data,\n                                  std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) override;\n\n```\n\n### 4. `util/focaltech/libusb_transport.cc`\n\nThis is the **only** place where the `static_cast` occurs now, safely quarantining the `libusb` C-API types.\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e LibusbTransport::Send(\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data, std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) {\n  auto open_res \u003d EnsureOpened();\n  if (!open_res) return std::unexpected(open_res.error());\n\n  int actual \u003d 0;\n  int r \u003d libusb_bulk_transfer(handle_.get(), endpoint_out_,\n                               const_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e(data.data()),\n                               static_cast\u003cint\u003e(data.size()), \u0026actual,\n                               static_cast\u003cunsigned int\u003e(timeout.count()));\n  if (r !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) return HandleTransferError(r);\n  \n  // Cast the libusb int to standard size_t here\n  return static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(actual);\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e LibusbTransport::Recv(\n    std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) {\n  auto open_res \u003d EnsureOpened();\n  if (!open_res) return std::unexpected(open_res.error());\n\n  int actual \u003d 0;\n  int r \u003d libusb_bulk_transfer(handle_.get(), endpoint_in_, data.data(),\n                               static_cast\u003cint\u003e(data.size()), \u0026actual,\n                               static_cast\u003cunsigned int\u003e(timeout.count()));\n  if (r !\u003d LIBUSB_SUCCESS) return HandleTransferError(r);\n  \n  // Cast the libusb int to standard size_t here\n  return static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(std::min(actual, static_cast\u003cint\u003e(data.size())));\n}\n\n```\n\n### 5. `util/focaltech/ft_scsi.cc`\n\nRemove the ugly `static_cast\u003cint\u003e` boilerplate from your core logic.\n\n```cpp\n// In SendBulkDataOut:\n  if (!data_buffer.empty()) {\n    auto send_res \u003d device.Send(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n    if (!send_res) {\n      return std::unexpected(send_res.error());\n    }\n    // CLEANED UP: No more static_cast\u003cint\u003e\n    if (*send_res !\u003d data_buffer.size()) {\n      FT_LOGE(\"Data OUT transfer failed: short write.\");\n      return std::unexpected(Error::kResultFail);\n    }\n  }\n\n```\n\n```cpp\n// In ReceiveBulkDataIn:\n  if (!data_buffer.empty()) {\n    auto recv_res \u003d device.Recv(data_buffer, timeout_ms);\n    if (!recv_res) {\n      return std::unexpected(recv_res.error());\n    }\n    // CLEANED UP: No more static_cast\u003cint\u003e\n    if (*recv_res !\u003d data_buffer.size()) {\n      FT_LOGW(\"Data IN transfer length mismatch (expected {}, got {})\",\n              data_buffer.size(), *recv_res);\n    }\n  }\n\n```\n\n### 6. `util/focaltech/mock_usb_transport.h`\n\nUpdate the GTest macros.\n\n```cpp\n  MOCK_METHOD((std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e), Send,\n              (std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e, std::chrono::milliseconds),\n              (override));\n  MOCK_METHOD((std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e), Recv,\n              (std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e, std::chrono::milliseconds), (override));\n\n```\n\n### 7. Update Fakes in Test Files\n\n**In `util/focaltech/cli_test.cc`:**\n\n```cpp\n// In FakeEcTransport\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Send(...) override {\n  // ...\n  return data.size(); // Remove static_cast\u003cint\u003e\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Recv(...) override {\n  // ...\n  return to_copy; // Remove static_cast\u003cint\u003e\n}\n\n// In FakeForFlashWp and FakeForSetWp\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Send(...) override {\n  // ...\n  return data.size(); // Remove static_cast\u003cint\u003e\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Recv(...) override {\n  // ...\n  return testing::kUsbCswSize; // (Or kFlashWpBufferSize)\n}\n\n```\n\n**In `util/focaltech/updater_test.cc`:**\n\n```cpp\n// In StubUsbTransport\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Send(...) override {\n  // ...\n  return data.size(); // Remove static_cast\u003cint\u003e\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e Recv(...) override {\n  // ...\n  return SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH; // (Or other returns, all implicitly size_t)\n}\n\n```\n\n**In `util/focaltech/usb_device_test.cc`:**\n\n```cpp\n// In RecvForwardsToTransport\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock_, Recv(_, timeout))\n      .WillOnce(Invoke([\u0026](std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e data, auto) {\n        std::fill(data.begin(), data.begin() + 5, 0xAB);\n        return std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e(5); // Update to size_t\n      }));\n\n  auto result \u003d device_-\u003eRecv(buffer, timeout);\n  ASSERT_TRUE(result.has_value());\n  EXPECT_EQ(*result, 5u); // Compare against unsigned literal\n\n```\n\n**In `util/focaltech/ft_scsi_test.cc`:**\nUpdate all the `Invoke` lambdas to return `size_t`. For example:\n\n```cpp\n  EXPECT_CALL(*mock, Send(_, _))\n      .WillOnce(Invoke([](auto, auto) -\u003e std::expected\u003csize_t, Error\u003e {\n        return testing::kUsbCbwSize;\n      }))\n\n```\n\n*(Note: If you took the earlier advice to simplify `Invoke` into just `Return(testing::kUsbCbwSize)`, you won\u0027t even need to update lambdas here — GTest will handle the type conversion automatically!)*",
