      "message": "Gemini feedback:\n\n---\n\nYou currently have four distinct structs defined solely to act as deleters for `libusb` types:\n\n```c\nstruct LibusbContextDeleter { void operator()(libusb_context* ctx) const; };\nstruct LibusbDeviceHandleDeleter { void operator()(libusb_device_handle* handle) const; };\n// ... etc\n\n```\n\n**Improvement:** You can delete all four of these structs and their implementations entirely. `std::unique_ptr` accepts free-function pointers directly via `decltype`. Since `std::unique_ptr` natively checks for `nullptr` before invoking the deleter, you can pass the libusb cleanup functions directly:\n\n```c\n// In libusb_transport.h, replace the custom types:\nusing ScopedContext \u003d std::unique_ptr\u003clibusb_context, decltype(\u0026libusb_exit)\u003e;\nusing ScopedDevice \u003d std::unique_ptr\u003clibusb_device, decltype(\u0026libusb_unref_device)\u003e;\nusing ScopedHandle \u003d std::unique_ptr\u003clibusb_device_handle, decltype(\u0026libusb_close)\u003e;\nusing ScopedConfig \u003d std::unique_ptr\u003clibusb_config_descriptor, decltype(\u0026libusb_free_config_descriptor)\u003e;\n\n// In libusb_transport.cc, instantiation becomes a one-liner:\nScopedContext ctx(raw_ctx, libusb_exit);\n\n```",
